Open Impact is an accredited spin-off of the University of Milano-Bicocca that provides services and develops digital products for measuring, enhancing and managing of impacts through an integrated sustainability approach. Open Impact was founded in 2019 thanks to the meeting of a mix of experiences and skills coming from the world of academic research, social innovation and digital development. By collecting and systematising a huge amount of internationally validated open- source impact assessments, Open Impact has managed to create the first database in Italy for im&shy; pact benchmarking. The Open Impact Database is designed to support organisations in identifying the impacts they generate, linking them to the 17 UN SGDs and other sustaina&shy; bility taxonomies, such as BES and ESG.

Services:
&middot; pact Strategy - We accompany organizations to recognize impact as a strategic asset and to build more desirable futures around it;
&middot; Impact Management - Through our digital platform we support organizations in ma&shy; naging the impact cycle of their initiatives, from the forecasting phases to the visualiza&shy; tion of their impact evidence;

&middot; Impact Research - Research is what we put as the starting and ending point of each of our processes;

&middot; Impact Investing - We support the construction of impact-oriented ecosystems and projects, promoting multistakeholder interaction to respond to complex social challen&shy; ges.

Products:

&middot; Impact measurement & management - We have developed digital tools that support impactmanagement, from the predictive phase to the automatic measurement and vi&shy; sualisation of data. The tools comply with the Impact Management standards.
&middot; Sustainability assessment & reporting - We have developed digital tools for reporting and assessing the sustainability of organisations.

Nova Reply (Business Unit of NET Reply SPA) is the Reply Group company whose mission is to guide its Customers in the Digital Transformation process for the adoption of next-generation networks, which will allow pervasively distributed connectivity.
The goal is to focus on the Aerospace and Defense markets, through a set of services which highlight on the following three offer segments:
1. Development of "Ubiquitous Networks", on terrestrial, space/satellite and submarine domains for the development of integrated connectivity solutions;
2. Creation of platforms and solutions for the orchestration of ubiquitous networks, for Network-as-a-Service applications;
3. Vertical applications: use cases and design, development and automation of services.
